# NiroWear public source — allowlist .gitignore
#
# The repository publishes application source and product documentation only.
# Everything else is excluded by DEFAULT and must be re-included deliberately,
# so a stray `git add .` cannot leak tests, prompts, evidence or credentials.

# 1. Exclude everything, then re-include what is published.
*
!*/

# 2. Build and tooling scaffolding that IS published.
!gradlew
!gradlew.bat
!build.gradle.kts
!settings.gradle.kts
!gradle.properties
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties
!gradle/gradle-daemon-jvm.properties
!secrets.properties.example
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!.editorconfig
# CI is published: a workflow nobody can see is not a gate.
!.github/workflows/*.yml
!.github/workflows/*.yaml
# A release workflow is often spelled .yaml; the blanket * would drop it silently.
# Repo infrastructure. The allowlist's blanket `*` silently swallowed these, which made
# "add Dependabot / SECURITY.md / CODEOWNERS" impossible without knowing to edit this file.
# Verified with: git check-ignore -v --no-index .github/dependabot.yml
!.github/dependabot.yml
!.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/**
!.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md
!SECURITY.md
!CODEOWNERS

# 3. Application source (main/debug/release only; never test sets).
!app/build.gradle.kts
!app/proguard-rules.pro
!app/schemas/**
!app/src/main/**
!app/src/debug/**
!app/src/release/**

# 4. Published documentation.
!README.md
!LICENSE
!AGENTS.md
!THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
!CONTRIBUTING.md
!docs/spec/**
!docs/adr/**
!docs/release/PRIVACY.md
!docs/release/BUILD_AND_RECOVERY.md
# Published release notes, one file per cut. A pinned name dropped the next release's notes
# SILENTLY: RELEASE_NOTES_0.1.1.md was written, `git add -A` reported a clean six-file commit, and
# only `git check-ignore -v` showed it missing. The glob keeps a cut's notes with its tag.
!docs/release/RELEASE_NOTES_*.md
!docs/release/CHANGELOG.md
!docs/memory/ARCHITECTURE.md
!docs/memory/PROVIDERS.md
!docs/memory/SCOPE.md
!docs/memory/RENDERER.md
!docs/memory/UI_RULES.md
!docs/branding/**
!docs/licenses/**
!docs/screenshots/**
!docs/index.html
!docs/changelog.html
!docs/.nojekyll
!fixtures/MATERIAL_ICONS_LICENSE.txt
!fixtures/MATERIAL_ICONS_NOTICE.txt
!fixtures/RENDER_TORTURE_FIXTURE.md

# 5. Hard exclusions that outrank every re-include above.
#    Test sources, prompts, handoffs, evidence and private material are never published.
#
#    The allowlist used to carry one exclusion line per historical session log (MEGA_*, HANDOFF*,
#    TEST_MATRIX, BETA3_*, ...). Those files were deleted on 2026-11-08 because nothing referenced
#    them; the blanket `*` above already excludes anything that reappears, so only the living
#    documents still on disk are named here.
app/src/test/
app/src/androidTest/
fixtures/.gitignore
docs/memory/DECISIONS.md
docs/memory/MATH_LICENSE_REVIEW.md
docs/memory/KNOWN_ISSUES.md
docs/memory/PROJECT.md
docs/memory/CREDENTIAL_ENTRY_DESIGN.md
artifacts/
artifactsbeta3-uiux-2026-10-18before/
scripts/*
# A negation cannot re-include a file inside an excluded DIRECTORY, so the directory pattern is
# narrowed to its contents first. These two are the gate runners CONTRIBUTING and the PR template
# tell contributors to use; they contain no credentials or local paths.
!scripts/disposable-instrumentation.ps1
!scripts/test-clean-wear.py
.private/
build/
.gradle/
.kotlin/
.idea/
*.iml
local.properties
secrets.properties
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p12
*.pfx
*.key
*.pem
*.apk
*.aab
*.hprof
*.log
.env
.env.*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.cxx/
.externalNativeBuild/
